      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
        "text": "## VHS Tape - analog degradation\n\nTwo branches, same node, different signal quality:\n\n- **1 - Tape signal** (top): `RetroColorDepth` crushes the image to 24 levels per channel - the soft quantisation of a tape recording - then `RetroVHS` adds chroma bleed, row jitter, noise and a rolling brightening band.\n- **2 - Direct signal** (bottom): the raw photo through a milder `RetroVHS`, for comparison.\n\n**Seeds:** `seed 0` = fresh randomness every run; `seed 42` = deterministic. Switch `noise_mode` to `mono` for gray grain instead of RGB confetti."
      },
      "widgets_values": [
